   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 1. Why Adaptive Beamforming?\n",
    "\n",
    "### Limitations of Fixed Beamforming (Delay-and-Sum)\n",
    "\n",
    "Fixed beamformers have several limitations:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Fixed pattern**: Cannot adapt to changing noise conditions\n",
    "2. **Limited noise rejection**: Only ~3 dB improvement for 2 mics\n",
    "3. **No directional nulling**: Cannot suppress specific interferers\n",
    "4. **Poor with directional noise**: Enhances noise from target direction\n",
    "\n",
    "### Adaptive Beamforming Philosophy\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Idea**: Learn from the data!\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Fixed Beamformer:              Adaptive Beamformer:\n",
    "  Mic1 ──[w₁=0.5]──┐             Mic1 ──[w₁(t,f)]──┐\n",
    "                   ├──→ Out                         ├──→ Out\n",
    "  Mic2 ──[w₂=0.5]──┘             Mic2 ──[w₂(t,f)]──┘\n",
    "                                        ↑\n",
    "  Fixed weights              [Learn from noise statistics]\n",
    "                             [Adapt to suppress interferers]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### MVDR: Minimum Variance Distortionless Response\n",
    "\n",
    "**Optimization Goal:**\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\min_{\\mathbf{w}} \\quad \\mathbf{w}^H \\mathbf{R} \\mathbf{w}$$\n",
    "$$\\text{subject to} \\quad \\mathbf{w}^H \\mathbf{a} = 1$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "- $\\mathbf{w}$ = weight vector (what we optimize)\n",
    "- $\\mathbf{R}$ = covariance matrix (noise statistics)\n",
    "- $\\mathbf{a}$ = steering vector (target direction)\n",
    "- **Minimize**: Output power (variance)\n",
    "- **Constraint**: Preserve signal from target direction\n",
    "\n",
    "**Result**: Can achieve 10-20 dB improvement!\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Steering Vector: The \"Signature\" of a Direction\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.1 What is a Steering Vector?\n",
    "\n",
    "The **steering vector** $\\mathbf{a}(\\theta, f)$ describes **how a plane wave from direction $\\theta$ appears at each microphone**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Physical Intuition:**\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Sound from angle θ\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "       / \\\n",
    "      /   \\\n",
    "     /     \\\n",
    "  Mic1    Mic2\n",
    "  \n",
    "Mic1 sees: amplitude × e^(jφ₁)\n",
    "Mic2 sees: amplitude × e^(jφ₂)\n",
    "\n",
    "Steering vector: a = [e^(jφ₁), e^(jφ₂)]ᵀ\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Mathematical Definition\n",
    "\n",
    "For a linear array with M microphones:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{a}(\\theta, f) = \\begin{bmatrix} e^{-j2\\pi f \\tau_1} \\\\ e^{-j2\\pi f \\tau_2} \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ e^{-j2\\pi f \\tau_M} \\end{bmatrix}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "- $\\tau_m = \\frac{d_m \\cdot \\sin(\\theta)}{c}$ = time delay to mic $m$\n",
    "- $d_m$ = distance of mic $m$ from reference\n",
    "- $f$ = frequency\n",
    "\n",
    "**For 2 mics (spacing $d$):**\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{a}(\\theta, f) = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ e^{-j2\\pi f \\frac{d \\sin(\\theta)}{c}} \\end{bmatrix}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def compute_steering_vector(mic_positions, theta_deg, freq, c=SPEED_OF_SOUND):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Compute steering vector for given direction and frequency.\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        mic_positions: Array of mic positions [M × 2] (x, y coordinates)\n",
    "        theta_deg: Direction of arrival (degrees, 0° = front)\n",
    "        freq: Frequency (Hz)\n",
    "        c: Speed of sound (m/s)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "        a: Steering vector [M × 1] (complex)\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    M = len(mic_positions)\n",
    "    theta_rad = np.radians(theta_deg)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Direction vector\n",
    "    direction = np.array([np.cos(theta_rad), np.sin(theta_rad)])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Time delays for each mic (relative to first mic)\n",
    "    tau = np.dot(mic_positions, direction) / c\n",
    "    tau = tau - tau[0]  # Make first mic the reference\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Steering vector (phase shifts)\n",
    "    omega = 2 * np.pi * freq\n",
    "    a = np.exp(-1j * omega * tau)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return a\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Steering vector computation function defined!\")"
   ]
  },
