    "---\n",
    "## 3. Covariance Matrix R: Noise Statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1 What is the Covariance Matrix?\n",
    "\n",
    "The **covariance matrix** $\\mathbf{R}$ captures the **statistical relationship** between microphone signals.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Definition:**\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{R} = E[\\mathbf{X} \\mathbf{X}^H]$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "- $\\mathbf{X} = [X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_M]^T$ = microphone signals (frequency domain)\n",
    "- $E[\\cdot]$ = expected value (average over time)\n",
    "- $\\mathbf{X}^H$ = conjugate transpose\n",
    "\n",
    "**For 2 mics:**\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{R} = \\begin{bmatrix} E[|X_1|^2] & E[X_1 X_2^*] \\\\ E[X_2 X_1^*] & E[|X_2|^2] \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} R_{11} & R_{12} \\\\ R_{21} & R_{22} \\end{bmatrix}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Physical Meaning:**\n",
    "- **Diagonal** ($R_{ii}$): Power at mic $i$\n",
    "- **Off-diagonal** ($R_{ij}$): Correlation between mics $i$ and $j$\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.2 Estimation\n",
    "\n",
    "In practice, we estimate $\\mathbf{R}$ from data:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Batch estimation:**\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{R} = \\frac{1}{T} \\sum_{t=1}^{T} \\mathbf{X}(t) \\mathbf{X}^H(t)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Exponential averaging (online):**\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{R}[n] = \\alpha \\mathbf{R}[n-1] + (1-\\alpha) \\mathbf{X}[n] \\mathbf{X}^H[n]$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where $\\alpha \\approx 0.95$ (smoothing factor)\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def estimate_covariance_matrix(X):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Estimate covariance matrix from microphone signals.\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        X: Microphone signals [M mics × T time frames]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "        R: Covariance matrix [M × M]\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    M, T = X.shape\n",
    "    R = (X @ X.conj().T) / T\n",
    "    return R\n",
    "\n",
    "def visualize_covariance_matrix(R, title=\"Covariance Matrix\"):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Visualize covariance matrix as heatmap.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 5))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Magnitude\n",
    "    ax = axes[0]\n",
    "    im = ax.imshow(np.abs(R), cmap='viridis', aspect='auto')\n",
    "    ax.set_title('Magnitude |R|', fontsize=12, weight='bold')\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('Microphone', fontsize=11)\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel('Microphone', fontsize=11)\n",
    "    plt.colorbar(im, ax=ax)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Add values\n",
    "    for i in range(R.shape[0]):\n",
    "        for j in range(R.shape[1]):\n",
    "            ax.text(j, i, f'{np.abs(R[i,j]):.2f}',\n",
    "                   ha='center', va='center', color='white', fontsize=11, weight='bold')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Phase\n",
    "    ax = axes[1]\n",
    "    im = ax.imshow(np.angle(R, deg=True), cmap='twilight', aspect='auto', vmin=-180, vmax=180)\n",
    "    ax.set_title('Phase ∠R (degrees)', fontsize=12, weight='bold')\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('Microphone', fontsize=11)\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel('Microphone', fontsize=11)\n",
    "    plt.colorbar(im, ax=ax)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Add values\n",
    "    for i in range(R.shape[0]):\n",
    "        for j in range(R.shape[1]):\n",
    "            ax.text(j, i, f'{np.angle(R[i,j], deg=True):.0f}°',\n",
    "                   ha='center', va='center', color='white', fontsize=10, weight='bold')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Real part\n",
    "    ax = axes[2]\n",
    "    im = ax.imshow(R.real, cmap='RdBu_r', aspect='auto')\n",
    "    ax.set_title('Real Part Re(R)', fontsize=12, weight='bold')\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('Microphone', fontsize=11)\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel('Microphone', fontsize=11)\n",
    "    plt.colorbar(im, ax=ax)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Add values\n",
    "    for i in range(R.shape[0]):\n",
    "        for j in range(R.shape[1]):\n",
    "            ax.text(j, i, f'{R[i,j].real:.2f}',\n",
    "                   ha='center', va='center', color='black', fontsize=11, weight='bold')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    plt.suptitle(title, fontsize=14, weight='bold', y=1.02)\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Covariance matrix functions defined!\")"
   ]
